WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:02.330
So much for keeping secrets.

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:06.890
Ever since they witnessed half of their favorite
superheroes disintegrate in Avengers: Infinity

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:10.600
War, Marvel fans have been on their edge of
their seats wondering how things will turn

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.360
out in the fourth Avengers movie.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.240
After what felt like an eternity, Marvel Studios
released the movie's first trailer in December

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.120
2018, revealing the title of the film to be
Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.520
But when the studio dropped the footage, it
also broke a few hearts — the first look

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:27.839
at the film was hardly a triumphant one.

00:00:27.839 --> 00:00:32.650
The teaser showed Robert Downey Jr.'s Tony
Stark floating aimlessly through space, low

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.960
on food and oxygen, and seemingly preparing
to die.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.760
Instead of rallying for a vengeful strike
against Thanos, his nemesis, the only glimpse

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.400
we saw of Iron Man was him recording a farewell
message to fiancée Pepper Potts.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.340
While some began preparing to say goodbye
to the billionaire bad boy, others started

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.420
speculating that another hero would swoop
in to save Tony from the brink of certain

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:53.920
death.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:59.420
One theory assembled evidence that Pepper
herself would do the saving, by finally assuming

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:03.540
her comic book alter ego of Rescue to somehow
bring her beau back home.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:09.420
"Just for the record Being adrift with no
hope of rescue is more fun than it sounds."

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.260
But a recent announcement from the car company
Audi may have inadvertently spoiled who will

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.240
actually save Tony's life in Endgame.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.790
During a presentation at January 2019's Consumer
Electronics Show, Audi announced that it had

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:25.520
partnered with Marvel to develop a VR experience
that ties in with Endgame.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.350
The cross-promotion will allow fans to venture
through space from the backseat of Audi's

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.630
e-tron Vision Gran Turismo.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.810
The vehicle will be making an appearance in
Endgame, supposedly with an alive-and-well

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.300
Tony Stark behind the wheel.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.020
"Well you have driven it already?”

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.560
"Yeah, well as Tony Stark on Avengers 4"

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.560
This development seemed to confirm that Tony
will make his way back to Earth in the fourth

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:52.460
Avengers adventure, and in good enough condition
to feel like zipping around in a sweet luxury

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:52.980
two-seater.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:58.300
The idea that Tony will survive his jaunt
through space, if true, barely feels like

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:58.960
a spoiler.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.080
It never seemed likely that he'd actually
die out there.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.280
But an important question remained: who would
be the one to rescue him?

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:10.080
Aspects of Audi's promotion strongly suggest
that the hero who saves Tony might be none

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.530
other than Rocket Raccoon — which would
surely come as a hallucinatory experience

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.260
for the oxygen-starved, dehydrated Earthling.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:22.520
The details are all in the title of Audi's
VR experience, "Marvel's Avengers: Rocket's

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:23.180
Rescue Run."

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:28.440
The game will apparently have players slide
into the e-tron GT's backseat, where they'll

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.020
control another vehicle as though they were
Rocket on a space-faring rescue mission.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.739
Though the name of the game alone doesn't
specify who Rocket is rescuing, it certainly

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.700
implies that Rocket might be the one who comes
to Tony's aid.

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:45.920
Tony is in Rocket's spaceship, after all — and
at the start of Avengers: Endgame, it would

00:02:45.921 --> 00:02:48.450
appear that he'll need rescuing more than
anyone else.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.220
Well, as long as we're not counting the people
who got dusted.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.430
Did Audi really release promotional details
that spoil this aspect of Endgame?

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:01.230
Thanks to an in-depth account of "Rescue Run"
from The Verge writer Sean O'Kane, it appears

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.300
pretty likely that that's exactly what's happened.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.960
In a piece published on January 7th, just
ahead of Audi's presentation at CES, O'Kane

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:08.460
wrote,

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.820
"Iron Man needs help.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.540
He's being chased through outer space by some
of Thanos' baddies, so Rocket Raccoon and

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.700
I rush to his aid.

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:20.620
We make a few jumps using the Universal Neural
Teleportation Network, and a few rollicking

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:24.000
minutes later, I've helped blast the enemies
to bits."

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.610
Small leaks about potential plot details happen
all the time with movies this high-profile,

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:33.140
but it's pretty wild to think that the famously
unforthcoming Marvel might have let this spoiler

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:33.640
slip.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:38.340
It's possible that the studio could have revealed
this info as a fakeout, as they've done before,

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.300
putting out misleading information to muddy
the waters when it comes to actual leaks.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:48.060
On the flip side, it's also possible that
this reveal is genuinely a marketing miscalculation

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.980
that reveals too much too soon.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:54.880
Both possibilities seem equally likely, and
are sure to fuel online debate as the movie's

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.980
much-anticipated release draws closer.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:02.239
As things stand now, there's a solid chance
that Endgame will see the galaxy's most beloved

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:07.200
trash panda head to space, save Tony, and
haul him back to Earth to reunite with the

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.420
other surviving heroes.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:12.880
Then they can formulate a plan to take down
Thanos, revive the fallen heroes, and then

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.440
take a joy ride in his cool new whip to celebrate
a job well done.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.520
I cannot believe it I haven’t driven one of these
in a while."

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.640
So — does this theory hold water?

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:26.640
From a story standpoint, Rocket saving Tony
would make a lot of sense.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:31.350
The Endgame trailer revealed that Tony and
Nebula will escape Titan onboard the Benatar,

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.380
the ship Star-Lord commandeered.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:38.199
The last time we saw Rocket, he was stranded
on Earth in Wakanda, watching helplessly as

00:04:38.199 --> 00:04:41.880
several heroes, including his best buddy Groot,
fell away to nothingness.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.490
He's the only Guardian to have made it out
of Thanos' decimation with his life intact,

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:49.220
but at the end of Infinity War, he has no
way of knowing that.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:53.320
So it's reasonable that Rocket will start
off Endgame fiercely determined to locate

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:57.860
his missing teammates — and where else would
he start looking for them than their own spaceship?

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.790
As plausible as all this sounds, right now
it's only a theory, and no one outside of

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:04.580
Marvel knows for sure how Tony will make it
back home.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:08.960
We'll keep our eye on the developments, but
the only way to be sure what really happens

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.400
will be to wait patiently for the movie's
premiere on April 26th.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:13.380
What's your secret?

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:13.880
Mellow jazz?

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:14.460
Bongo drums?

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:14.860
Huge bag?"

